@ajratner @xeophon @vincentsunnchen Not trying to single out TB (I haven't looked at that one closely yet but will).  But I can tell you that the average benchmark quality is surprisingly bad for the ones that I have checked, which makes me skeptical in general  

I am just advocating the value in being super skeptical, running bench yourself, and looking at the traces where the grader fails it (which is what I said).  This is because when I have done this analysis I've found that these tend to correlate highly with ill specified questions, bad graders, bad assertions, or unrealistic situations or poor harness design and the only way to pass is to "memorize that thing", rather than real signal about model intelligence, MUCH more than I previously would have thought.  

I am just shocked that is all.  Everyone I know that has done this exercise of looking at the data shares the same sentiment.  So I think its time to shine light on this phenomenon of BenchmarkGate.  It will take some work though to do systematically.

